## VERDICT: PASS

(iteration 2; iteration 1 was a VETO by the independent reviewer)

---

### Executive Summary

Phase 239 imports the admitted P1 /qor-roadmap capability (prototype commit 31243902) onto current main under the plan's fail-closed promotion rule, with declared base-motion deviations only (Skills badge 31 to 32; FEATURE_INDEX renumbered FX026 to FX027). Iteration 1: the independent reviewer confirmed exact contract fidelity on every clause except one and VETOed on it - a second node_resolved event for an already-resolved node was accepted end-to-end from the shipped CLI, silently replacing recorded rationale/authority/evidence: de-facto decision supersession, which the plan's non_goals, the admitted contract, and the skill's own text all exclude. Iteration 2 closed it with a status guard mirroring _space_retired (red-proved), plus behavioral coverage for the contract's previously untested duplicate-identity and sequence-gap clauses; the reviewer independently re-verified the fix and lifted the VETO, noting the guard fires for all node kinds.

### Iteration 1 findings (independent reviewer; VETO)

- Blocking (specification-drift): _node_resolved lacked an already-resolved guard; re-resolution reachable via resolve -> append_payload -> reduce_events with unchanged authority. Fact evidence pointers equally replaceable.
- Secondary (coverage-gap): duplicate identities and sequence gaps were implemented as rejections but untested.

### Iteration 2 remediation (verified by the reviewer at source)

- Guard added before kind-specific checks (fires for fact/decision/prerequisite); red-proof executed. test_re_resolution_is_rejected_as_supersession isolates the guard from the authority check.
- test_duplicate_identities_and_sequence_gaps_are_rejected covers duplicate node id, duplicate event_id (made discriminating per the reviewer's follow-up: distinct node id so only the event_id collides, match tightened to "duplicate event_id"), and non-contiguous seq.
- Also closed at this iteration: the plan gained its Phase 38 contract "## CI Commands" section (the pre-authored plan predated the check's expectations on this branch), and SKILL_REGISTRY's meta category count advanced to 14.

### Reviewer confirmations recorded

Contract fidelity exact on all other clauses (seven event kinds, three node kinds, evidence/authority rules, confined store path with double-layer containment, atomic replace, fail-closed scope handoff ending at /qor-plan, no ranking or auto-selection, no production implementation procedure in the skill). Security clean; razor met (all modules <= 232 lines, functions <= 24). Shared surfaces consistent (delegation routes only to ideate/research/plan; FX027 cites a real invoking test; badge 32 matches the 32 SKILL.md files on disk). Publication boundary clean including the carried design docs. Non-blocking observations recorded as accepted pilot-scale trade-offs for GH #373's evaluation: unreachable containment branch as defense-in-depth, no fsync before replace, quadratic full-file rewrite vs append-only framing, private imports in roadmap_view.

